w: 1.~Sing, O sing, this bless- ed morn, Un- to us a Child is born, 
w: 2.~Je- sus Christ, the King of kings, Ma- ker of all world- ly things,
w: 3.~God of God, and Light of Light, Comes with mer- cies in- fi- nite;
w: 4.~God with us, Em- man- u- el, Deigns for ev- er now to dwell;
w: 5.~Truth and Mer- cy show their face, And with lov- ing kiss em- brace;
w: 6.~God comes down that man may rise, Lift- ed far a- bove the skies
w: 7.~Hu- man flesh is now be- come Christ's a- bode, the God- head's home;
w: 8.~Now we rise, from pri- son free; On we march to vic- to- ry,
w: 9.~Now be- hold the ris- ing Sun Hath His glor- ious race be- gun;
w: 10.~O re- new us, Lord, we pray, With Thy Spi- rit day by day;
w: 11.~Sing, O sing this bless- ed Morn, Je- sus Christ to\-- day is born;
